## 3. The Matter Content

The 16-spinor of SO(10) decomposes under the Standard Model gauge group
into exactly one generation of fermions:

16 → (3,2){1/6} + (3,1){2/3} + (3,1)_{−1/3}

(1,2){−1/2} + (1,1){−1} + (1,1)_0


The first term is the left-handed quark doublet: six states, three
colors times two isospin states. The next two terms are the right-handed
up-type and down-type quarks: three states each. The fourth term is the
left-handed lepton doublet: two states. The fifth is the right-handed
electron. The sixth is the right-handed neutrino.

The total is sixteen. Six plus three plus three plus two plus one plus
one equals sixteen.

This is one full generation of Standard Model fermions, with the
right-handed neutrino included. Every quantum number — color, isospin,
hypercharge, electric charge, baryon number minus lepton number — is
contained in this decomposition. The electric charges that emerge are
{+2/3, −1/3, 0, −1}, exactly the charges observed in the Standard Model.

The anomaly cancellation conditions — Tr(B−L) = 0 and Tr(Y) = 0 — are
satisfied exactly, by integer arithmetic, without any free parameters.

**The matter content of one generation is not assumed. It is the
decomposition of a single mathematical object: the 16-spinor of SO(10),
selected by the partition structure of the dimension.**

