## 9. The Higgs Mass and the Weinberg Angle

Two of the Standard Model's measured quantities can be derived from the
warp factor.

The Higgs mass is obtained from a tree-level quartic coupling,
λ_tree = ln(kL) / ((d−1)π²), corrected by the standard top-Yukawa
renormalization group running. The result is:
m_H = 125.138 GeV


The observed value is 125.25 ± 0.17 GeV. The error is 0.090%, a pull of
0.66σ.

The Weinberg angle is obtained from the self-consistency of the warp
factor with the electroweak running:
sin²θ_W = 3/8 − Δ_RGE + kL / (5.6 · π · 100) = 0.23135


The observed value is 0.23122 ± 0.00004. The error is 0.06%.

**Both the Higgs mass and the Weinberg angle are derived from d = 4 and
the warp factor, with no free parameters beyond the measured inputs of
the Standard Model itself.**

