## 11. The Thesis

The Standard Model is a theorem about the number 4.

The dimension of spacetime is the only input. From it, by arithmetic
alone, the following are derived: the size and geometry of the
substrate; the gauge group SO(10) and its Standard Model subgroup; the
generation content and its multiplet structure; the three generations;
the 14 particles of one generation; the warp factor, the Higgs mass, and
the Weinberg angle; and the self-cancellation of the vacuum energy.

What is not derived — the specific particle masses and the flavor
mixings — is empirical, as it is in every framework.

The universe is four-dimensional. Everything else follows.

